525: The fourth formal root combination, good \(III^*\) and good II,
526: has both orders even. Its determinant is even and it contains
527: no sphere tuple. No sphere return class is assigned to it.
528: 
529: For F38, the source is \(I_1^*+IV+I_1\), with \(d=12\).
530: At infinity \(m_\infty=2\), the actual root is \(I_2\),
531: and \(e_\infty'=2\). Its page consists of \(m_0\) copies of this
532: root and two copies of the IV root. The two sectors are:
533: 
534: | \((a,b)\) | \(m_\infty\) at \(I_1^*\) | \(m_0\) at IV | Actual \(A^{\rm Jin}\) |
535: |---|---|---|---|
536: | \((6,2)\) | \(2\), root \(I_2\) | \(6l+1\), reduced IV | \(-16l-2\) |
537: | \((2,6)\) | \(2\), root \(I_2\) | \(3k\), good, \(k\) odd | \(0\) |
538: 
539: Here the sphere equation is \(m_0n_\infty+2n_0=\pm1\).
540: It forces \(m_0\) odd; together with the reduced root domain
541: \(m_0\equiv1\pmod3\), this gives the stated \(6l+1\).
542: Equation (K28.28) is \(\chi=(2m_0+e_0')/6\).
543: In the reduced row (K28.29) gives
544: \(c_1(N)^2=-6m_0\), and hence
545: \(A=(2-8m_0)/3=-16l-2\). In the good row it gives
546: \(h(aG')=2m_0/3\) and \(\chi=m_0/3\), hence zero.
547: 
548: Finally consider the single quadratic \(I_1^*\) cap of F36
549: on either \(I_1^*+I_3+2I_1\) or \(I_1^*+IV+I_1\).
550: Here \((a,b)=(6,2)\), \(\lambda=r^2\), and \(n=\pm1\).
551: The exact one-cap map of K26, with \(m=2\), gives the complex
552: page \(\eta-\tau\xi^2=1\) and the positive Hopf angle \(n\gamma\).
553: The root sheet and its actual line are precisely (K28.20)--(K28.22).
554: The integral page coinvariants vanish by the one-cap argument
555: of K26: the retained meridians recover the whole source
556: monodromy, and a nonzero prime quotient of its coinvariants
557: would give a nonzero rational torsion section, contradicting
558: the proved source Mordell--Weil group \(\mathbb Z\).
559: Thus the same relative line and signed Thom maps apply.
560: The Euler count is
561: \[
562:               \chi=\frac{2(12-7)+2}{12}=1,\qquad
563:               h(6G')=\frac{2\cdot36}{12}=6 .
564: \]
565: The remaining \(I_3\) or IV component correction is zero for
566: \(6G'\). It follows that the actual return is
567: \[
568:                        A^{\rm Jin}=-2
569:  \tag{K28.31}
570: \]
571: for either norm sign and for both source profiles.
572: 
573: By the exact transfer P3F.22, the physical Hopf-gluing class of
574: every row is \(A^{\rm Jin}\bmod28\), with
575: \(\mu=A^{\rm Jin}/28\bmod\mathbb Z\). A nonzero residue has the
576: nonproduct mapping torus proved in P3F.24. The present proof
577: uses the actual norm, page, line and trace maps before applying
578: that transfer.
579: 
